# Frontend rules

## Routes (`App.jsx`)

| Path | Page |
|------|------|
| `/` | Landing |
| `/hub` | Agent Hub (dashboard) |
| `/agents/:agentId` | New agent thread |
| `/agents/:agentId/threads/:threadId` | Workspace |
| `/chat` | Classic concierge |
| `/owner` | Owner dashboard |

## API client

- `frontend/src/utils/api.js` — Axios + SSE helpers
- Base URL: `VITE_API_BASE_URL` (must end with `/api`)
- Auth: `configureApiAuth()` from `authStore.jsx`

## Trip pack UI

- `TripPackPanel.jsx` on `AgentHubPage` — shows when `profile_complete`; buttons when `trip_pack_ready`
- `tripPackAPI.getSummary()`, `downloadPdf()`, `sendEmail()`

## Artifact components

- `PackageCard.jsx`, `FoodGuideCard.jsx`, `ItineraryTimeline.jsx`
- Normalize artifacts via `utils/agentArtifacts.js`

## Styling

- Tailwind; brand: `forest`, `gold`, `cream`
- Framer Motion for hub cards; respect reduced-motion where possible

## Food images

- URLs like `/images/food/Hoppers.jpg` from Vite `public/`
- `FoodGuideCard` shows photos from `dish.image.url` — not in chat markdown

## Do not

- Put API keys in frontend code
- Use class components
- Call backend directly (always via BFF in browser)
